========================================================
SECTION 7 - OPTIONAL: SHOW ACTION COUNT ON THE CALENDAR
========================================================

Right now every pill reads "EMEA Bi-Weekly Sync" because
every meeting in a region has the same title. That text
carries no information. Show the action count instead.

7.1  lblLoadData -> OnSelect   (replace whole property)

ClearCollect(
    colMeetings,
    Filter('Meeting Notes', Region = varCalRegion.Value)
);
ClearCollect(
    colCalEvents,
    ForAll(
        colMeetings As M,
        {
            EventDate: DateValue(Text(M.'Meeting Date', "yyyy-mm-dd")),
            Title: M.Title,
            ActionCount: CountRows(M.'Meeting Action Items'),
            OpenCount: CountRows(
                Filter(
                    M.'Meeting Action Items',
                    Text('Status (psquad_status)') <> "Completed"
                )
            )
        }
    )
)

7.2  galCalendar -> Items
     Inside the innermost record, add two lines after
     TopTitle:

        TopActions: First(_evts).ActionCount,
        TopOpen: First(_evts).OpenCount,

7.3  lblEvtTitle -> Text
If(
    ThisItem.TopActions > 0,
    ThisItem.TopActions & If(ThisItem.TopActions = 1, " action", " actions"),
    "Notes only"
)

7.4  recEvtAccent -> Fill
If(
    ThisItem.TopOpen > 0,
    RGBA(245, 158, 11, 1),
    RGBA(22, 163, 74, 1)
)

     Amber bar = open actions outstanding.
     Green bar  = everything closed.
     Now the calendar tells you where work is pending at
     a glance, which is the actual point of the screen.


========================================================
NOTE ON ROUNDED CORNERS
========================================================
Rectangle@2.3.0 in your tenant has no Radius properties,
so cards and pills stay square. Two ways round it if you
want them rounded later:

  - Image@2.2.3 supports RadiusTopLeft etc. An Image with
    no image set and a Fill is a rounded rectangle.
  - ModernTextInput@1.1.1 also exposes Radius.

Both are workarounds. Square corners are consistent and
fine - do this only if you decide it matters.
